{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And this stone.</b> I will offer sacrifices upon it and set aside tithes. The vav of 'והאבן' is superfluous: 'and HaShem will be לי לאלהים — as judge and avenger — והאבן הזאת.' And if you ask: how did Jacob make an altar of the stones that he had placed at his head? — we say at the end of Zevaḥim: an altar from which a layperson has not used the stones, etc. But one may answer: for a private altar (במת יחיד) there is no such stringency. 'It shall be a house of Elohim' — its place shall be a house of Elohim. And the word 'יהיה' does not refer back to 'אבן.' Another interpretation: we find masculine language used for a feminine noun: 'אך בגורל יחלק את הארץ' — 'אתן את הארץ הזאת' — and it does not say 'אותם הארץ.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "The text appears to cite two different biblical examples; the second citation 'אתן את הארץ הזאת' (Ezekiel 47:14) shows masculine 'אתן' governing feminine 'הארץ', while the first 'ולא נשא' is obscure in context and rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:34.209824843Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}